   "en": "The Gemara answers: «Even if you say» that the mishna is in accordance with the opinion of «Hillel,» we may distinguish between the cases such that there is no contradiction: «This» case, in which the mishna permits borrowing a loaf of bread as a loan, is applicable «in a place» where «the price» of the loaf «is set,» while «this» statement, which was said by Hillel, is applicable «in a place» where «its price is not set.»"
